// Applied projects and their datasets (§5 "real-world project bridges", §9
// "Offer dataset provenance and licensing; mark synthetic examples clearly";
// V4 §7: question → provenance → assumptions → method → code →
// interpretation → decision → limitations). The six V4 projects come first.
//
// Every dataset states where it comes from. Synthetic data are generated by
// code shown to the learner; the one real dataset (Anscombe’s quartet) is a
// published table of eleven numbers per series, reproduced from the 1973
// paper. Its values were checked against the paper’s published summary
// statistics (means, variances, fitted line, correlation) — see
// src/data/projects/__tests__/datasets.test.js.

